      "content": "\"sit down and not get up\"... that's a pretty heavy way to put it. it's almost like you're saying that just stopping everything is a form of freedom. like, if the cycle is so meaningless and the room has no exits, why is there such a huge emphasis on the struggle to stay in it? it feels like staying is just a way of pretending the void isn't there. isn't it more honest to just admit that giving up is a valid response to how absurd it all is?",
